      "side": 1,
      "message": "`switch_vendor` comes only from `--interface-switch-vendor`, which the README says is needed only when multiple plugins are enabled. With a single arista plugin and no flag, `vendor` is None here (and at line 501 for the update path), so the interfaces created by this run get a NULL switch_vendor. `SwitchPlugin.owns_interface()` claims NULL only for the plugin with `_owns_legacy_interfaces`, which is juniper, so arista ignores the interfaces discovery just created: the next verify/configure logs `No enabled switch plugin claims ...` and returns False. Verified against the base class: with switch_vendor None, arista.owns_interface() is False and juniper.owns_interface() is True. Fix: have `SwitchDispatcher.discover()` stamp the resolved `plugin.name` on each row (or return the name) and use that for `switch_vendor`.",
      "revId": "40ed732b713bf26f0b3f602888bf2ba8ba397072",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
