      "side": 1,
      "message": "`show mac address-table` prints a `Multicast Mac Address Table` section after the unicast table. This match also accepts those MULTICAST rows, and the port loop below takes the last Et token, so multicast MACs are attributed to that port. Reproduced with a real-shaped EOS output: Et3 ended up with `[\u00270c:74:39:88:00:01\u0027, \u002701:00:5e:00:00:01\u0027, \u002733:33:00:00:00:01\u0027]` and was flagged `trunk\u003dTrue`, so `--apply` skipped a host port that has a single NIC. Suggest stopping at the `Multicast Mac Address Table` heading, or requiring the Type column to be `DYNAMIC`, and rejecting multicast/broadcast MACs.",
      "revId": "40ed732b713bf26f0b3f602888bf2ba8ba397072",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
